@@ -1,5 +1,9 @@                                                                                                      
 # Living Survey: brain                                                                                              
                                                                                                                     
 ## Introduction                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
 This document collects the scientific literature regarding **brain**.                                               
+                                                                                                                    
+## Brain-Computer Interfaces and Neurophysiological Signal Processing                                               
+                                                                                                                    
+Recent advancements in brain-computer interfaces (BCIs) and neurophysiological signal processing have focused on    
improving classification accuracy, personalization, and reproducibility. Machine learning approaches, particularly   
Random Forest algorithms, have demonstrated robust performance in classifying EEG signals from real and imagery motor
activities, even with consumer-grade hardware, though interpersonal variability remains a challenge [^2609.11695]. To
standardize the analysis of brain dynamics, the open-source package pyAvalanches provides a complete pipeline for    
characterizing neuronal avalanches and their spatiotemporal propagation using EEG recordings [^2609.11530]. In the   
domain of P300 spellers, factorial experiments have revealed component anti-synergy, showing that combining          
individually promising filters and language models does not always yield additive performance gains, emphasizing the 
need for context-aware pipeline design [^2609.10961]. Federated learning frameworks like NEXUS-MI address the        
personalization bottleneck in motor-imagery BCIs by coordinating edge devices while minimizing communication overhead
[^2609.09786]. Furthermore, multimodal binding strategies such as EEGBind leverage synchronized video context to     
improve source-level classification of interictal epileptiform discharges from subtle EEG windows [^2609.09728].     
Beyond clinical applications, brain-based digital twins are being developed to fuse consumer-grade EEG with kinematic
data for real-time feedback in skilled motor tasks like cricket batting [^10.17870_bathspa.00017805], while infant   
EEG microstate analysis continues to uncover links between early temperament traits and global brain electrical      
activity [^10.7273_000007929].                                                                                       
+                                                                                                                    
+## Advanced Neuroimaging and Metastasis Detection                                                                   
+                                                                                                                    
+Volumetric segmentation and registration of brain structures continue to be driven by deep learning ensembles and   
diffusion models. For brain metastases, an nnU-Net ResEnc-L ensemble combined with rule-based post-processing has    
achieved state-of-the-art lesion-wise Dice scores on the BraTS 2026 benchmark, with rigorous out-of-fold validation  
confirming the robustness of specific processing stages [^2609.11477]. Scale-aware 3D deep learning frameworks       
utilizing cross-field-of-view probability fusion have also proven effective in reducing false positives while        
maintaining high precision in multimodal MRI metastasis detection [^2609.10825]. In developmental neuroscience, a    
trained deep registration pipeline now aligns Drosophila larval brain volumes to a reference template in a single    
forward pass, offering orders-of-magnitude speed improvements over classical deformable methods [^2609.11240].       
Diffeomorphic image registration has been advanced through a two-parameter flow map learning framework that enforces 
cocycle consistency, yielding improved alignment accuracy on brain MRI benchmarks without relying on numerical       
velocity integration [^2609.10789]. Additionally, the LUCID framework integrates multi-view diffusion priors with    
projection-domain data consistency to recover missing Fourier components in laminographic X-ray nanoimaging of       
mammalian brain tissue [^2609.10456]. Spatially resolved atlases of pan-cancer brain metastases are being constructed
using 10x Visium datasets, providing unprecedented single-cell and spatial context for tumor microenvironment        
analysis [^10.5281_zenodo.21816284][^10.5281_zenodo.21816285][^10.5281_zenodo.21782885][^10.5281_zenodo.21782884].   
Research into metastatic mechanisms also highlights RET signaling as a key mediator in estrogen receptor-positive    
breast cancer brain metastasis [^10.5281_zenodo.19501083][^10.5281_zenodo.19501082].                                 
+                                                                                                                    
+## Computational Neuroscience and Brain Network Dynamics                                                            
+                                                                                                                    
+Theoretical and computational models are increasingly bridging artificial intelligence with biological brain        
networks. The CoMA-DiT framework utilizes bidirectional cross-modal diffusion transformers to treat paired modalities
as mutual generative supervision sources, significantly enhancing multimodal brain state decoding [^2609.11341]. For 
MEG data, a regression-based framework employing Wendland radial basis functions and model-based gradient boosting   
provides spatially resolved cortical activation estimates, overcoming the limitations of traditional cluster-based   
permutation tests [^2609.11278]. The "Platonic brain bridge hypothesis" proposes that omni models processing video,  
audio, and text converge on brain-like representations, with human cortical networks serving as architectural priors 
that boost benchmark accuracy [^2609.10947]. Directed cortical signal flow during motor execution has been mapped    
using Permutation Transfer Entropy, demonstrating that inter-hemispheric information dynamics are functionally       
conserved across right- and left-handed individuals [^2609.10870]. Foundation models for fMRI are being optimized    
through BrainTaskonomy, which organizes pretraining and adaptation via measured learning relations and directed      
taskonomy routing [^2609.10518]. Theoretical work on neural activity models shows that criticality emerges naturally 
in large-scale systems without fine-tuning, as parameter space regions near critical points map to large observable  
statistics [^2609.09438]. Scalable neuronal reconstruction is addressed by SkNeXt, a topology-first framework that   
converts morphology into compact skeletons to drastically reduce computational overhead in petabyte-scale microscopy 
[^2609.09832]. Olfactory system research reveals a spatial code governing receptor choice that aligns sensory maps   
between the nose and brain [^10.5281_zenodo.18941307][^10.5281_zenodo.18941308], while gut-brain axis studies        
identify cholecystokinin signaling in the nucleus of the solitary tract as a local regulator of satiety              
[^10.7273_000008411]. Comprehensive arteriovenous metabolomics have also quantified inter-organ metabolite exchange, 
revealing significant brain-specific uptake and release patterns                                                     
[^10.5281_zenodo.20652506][^10.5281_zenodo.20652505].                                                                
+                                                                                                                    
+## Brain Aging, Neurodegeneration, and Biomarkers                                                                   
+                                                                                                                    
+Longitudinal modeling and explainable AI are refining brain age estimation and neurodegenerative biomarker          
discovery. Brain-PACE extends Siamese longitudinal frameworks to directly estimate structural brain aging pace from  
paired T1-weighted MRIs, showing stronger associations with tau burden and cognitive impairment than indirect        
cross-sectional methods [^2609.11378]. Covariance neural networks (VNNs) operating on graph representations of       
covariance matrices provide refined stability bounds and transferability characterizations, offering principled      
alternatives to PCA-based pipelines for brain age gap analysis in neurodegeneration [^2609.10490]. The XAI-Refine    
framework introduces an automated explanation-knowledge loop that iteratively aligns brain-age prediction models with
verified neurobiological literature through differentiable constraints [^2609.09388]. In Alzheimer's research, a     
critical evolutionary perspective argues against broad-spectrum amyloid precursor protein (APP) suppression,         
positioning APP as a universal pro-survival connector rather than merely a pathological substrate                    
[^10.5281_zenodo.20049820]. Cross-cultural studies on category fluency highlight how age-related gray matter volume  
changes in the DLPFC and MTL interact with culturally shaped cognitive strategies [^10.48617_etd.1671]. Furthermore, 
circular RNAs (circRNAs) have emerged as stable biological age markers in the Drosophila brain, with accumulation    
rates correlating to biological rather than chronological age [^10.48617_etd.1568]. Predicting blood-brain barrier   
(BBB) permeability remains crucial for CNS drug development; explainable machine learning frameworks using molecular 
descriptors have achieved high accuracy in identifying key physicochemical drivers like TPSA and LogP [^2609.10012], 
while quantum reservoir computing architectures utilizing discrete time crystals show promise in forecasting BBB     
permeability and electronic gaps [^2609.11071].                                                                      
+                                                                                                                    
+## Glioblastoma and Targeted Therapeutics                                                                           
+                                                                                                                    
+Glioblastoma (GBM) research is increasingly leveraging liquid biopsies, epigenetic profiling, and advanced          
nanomedicine. Nucleosome positioning analysis in cell-free DNA (cfDNA) from GBM patients reveals reproducible family-
and tissue-specific repositioning around transcription factor binding sites, offering non-invasive diagnostic        
potential [^10.5526_err-00042862]. Broader cfDNA repeat profiling establishes a comprehensive atlas of nucleosome    
signatures that successfully discriminate cancer patients from healthy controls across multiple tumor types,         
including GBM [^10.5526_err-00042900]. Therapeutic delivery across the blood-brain barrier is being advanced through 
lipid nanoparticle (LNP) platforms encapsulating siRNA targeting TERT, demonstrating robust gene silencing and       
cytotoxic effects in GBM cell lines [^10.17030_uclan.thesis.00059253]. Similarly, lipid-based nanostructured lipid   
carriers and lipid nanoparticles loaded with epigallocatechin gallate (EGCG) show promising colloidal stability and  
drug encapsulation rates for future GBM therapies [^10.17030_uclan.thesis.00059033]. At the cellular level,          
secretomes and extracellular vesicles (EVs) derived from neural crest stem cells significantly inhibit GBM           
proliferation and migration by modulating NF-κB activation and normalizing the anti-tumor immune microenvironment,   
highlighting their potential to overcome chemoresistance [^10.48683_1926.00128572].                                  
                                                                                                                     

